/death, /wishing, 1 /secret door detection, a few /digging, and all the
/teleport found/borrowed/stolen/polypiled throughout the game.  Maybe 1
/fire.  And 3-4 blessed !speed, so you can wear jumping boots on astral
and still be very fast (haste self works too but takes mana).

The /teleport are key.

> > I will wear the ring of protection on one hand, and the regeneration or
> > free action as need on the other.
>
> I'm gonna suggest you reverse your priorities there - Free Action is more
> important than regeneration (I think) - I'd keep it on all the time.  I'd
> probably go free action/regeneration, if I had the food to spare.

Free Action is mandatory.  On the planes, Conflict is the best other
option (and on Astral it's borderline essential).  The =protection
isn't that helpful at this point.

I'll sometimes wind up with =Free Action and =Teleport Control if I
haven't gotten TC intrinsically, but once you hit the (no-teleport)
planes, you can ditch =TC.

> > I want to enchant/fooproof the boots of levitation(I don't want to rely
> > on my ring it can explode).
>
> Not a bad idea; keep them in your bag.

I don't think there's anything that can explode your rings if you have
reflection, except things you initiate (and hence can avoid); e.g.
never throw Mjollnir (that it can be thrown is a trap for new players
IMO), don't loot chests that have traps on them (always #untrap several
times to be sure), etc.

> > Is there any adventage to using the fireproofed boots of water walking
> > over levitation? Should I even bring them?
>
> Not in vanilla nethack :)  Dump 'em!

They're good for dipping potions to dilute them (and scrolls) but
that's about it.

> > I understand that after you get the amulet, you get your items randomly
> > cursed, so you need to have things pre blessed and to have lots of holy
> > water. If I carry many light useless items, will they absorb some of the
> > curse attacks?
>
> Yes.  The extra slots being used might cause concern (if you suddenly need
> to pick up the 2 /oCreateMonster something dropped and suddenly couldn't
> pull out your /oW if you needed it immediately...)

Many people #name a bunch of K-rations to different things as curse
targets.

Carry /cancellation (not in the bag) as a backup if your bag of holding
gets cursed (drop the bag, zap it with /cancel and it reverts to
uncursed).  I also carry a sack with a blessed ?remove curse and a
couple !holy water.

